 "drivingQuestion": "What labor does one perform by striking the anvil?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Abaye and Rava's explanation stands, supported by a baraita",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.103a.3",
   "daf": "103a",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר: הַמַּכֶּה בְּקוּרְנָס עַל הַסַּדָּן כּוּ׳. מַאי קָעָבֵיד? רַבָּה וְרַב יוֹסֵף דְּאָמְרִי תַּרְוַיְיהוּ: מִפְּנֵי שֶׁמְאַמֵּן אֶת יָדוֹ. קָשׁוּ בָּהּ בְּנֵי רַחֲבָה: אֶלָּא מֵעַתָּה, חֲזָא אוּמָּנוּתָא בְּשַׁבְּתָא וּגְמַר, הָכִי נָמֵי דְּמִיחַיַּיב? אֶלָּא אַבָּיֵי וְרָבָא דְּאָמְרִי תַּרְוַיְיהוּ: שֶׁכֵּן מְרַדְּדֵי טַסֵּי מִשְׁכָּן עוֹשִׂין כֵּן. תַּנְיָא נָמֵי הָכִי, רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר: אַף הַמַּכֶּה בְּקוּרְנָס עַל הַסַּדָּן בִּשְׁעַת מְלָאכָה — חַיָּיב, שֶׁכֵּן מְרַדְּדֵי טַסֵּי מִשְׁכָּן עוֹשִׂין כֵּן.",
   "en": "We also learned in the mishna that «Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel says:» Even «one who strikes an anvil with a sledgehammer» is liable. The Gemara wonders: «What has he done» by striking the anvil that would render him liable? It was «Rabba and Rav Yosef who both said» in explanation: He is liable «because he trains his hand» for his work by striking the anvil. «The sons of» a man named «Raḥava» found «this» answer «difficult: If so, one who observed a craft» being performed «on Shabbat and learned» to perform that craft through observation, would «he also be liable?» Only one who performs an actual labor on Shabbat is liable. «Rather,» it was «Abaye and Rava who both said» in explanation: He is liable, «as those who flatten plates» of metal «for the Tabernacle do so.» They would strike the anvil with the sledgehammer in order to straighten the sledgehammer’s handle, which became crooked. «That was also taught» in a baraita. «Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel says: Even one who strikes an anvil with a sledgehammer during his labor is liable, as those who flatten plates» of metal «for the Tabernacle do so.»"
  }
 ],
